body:
A letter finds you by the ordinary post, which is how Wenna Aldric sends anything she means to be kept. You know the hand before you have read a word of it: it is the careful script that stops in the middle of your line in the Register. It has been corrected in two places, both times to make it more exact.

It reads:

"You never technically graduated. This is a defect in the record, and I correct defects. You will sit three examinations, set by me and marked by me. I have chosen them from what you have done least of since you came back, because that is what examinations are for.

"The first: {exam_task_1}

"The second, when the first is done: {exam_task_2}

"The third I will set in person.

"W. Aldric, Provost"

Below the signature a line has been begun and struck out. The strike is thorough, and almost complete. The first word escaped it: "Thank".

{remembrance}
